  "audit_finding_on_baseline_script": "In ceiling_suite/papers/recompute_p1_learners.py, burn_in_cohort() returned b_info containing the learned weights, but probe_settled_population() ignored b_info, initialized gains = np.ones(K), and used W_in * dphi_0 instead of theta_mlp. Moreover, q_profit_trained updated a scalar profit-gradient slope rather than a Bellman Q-table. This hardened script serializes and reloads the actual learned checkpoints and adds a genuine 21x21 tabular Bellman Q-learner with TD(0) backups.",
